<!-- TibannaEmbargo_CutMineableRoute.xml     RimUtinni · authored 2026-09-12

     TIBANNA_SOURCE_CUT_1 (CARD T1, RULED 2026-09-12: cut the violators).
     the_forge.md §6 hard ban 5: no tibanna source but the beldons — no
     mineral or synthetic route, ever. `tibanna_embargo_plot_spec.md`'s own
     survey found the live mod stack violating this in TWO ways: OuterRim
     core ships three extractor buildings (cut via Cherry Picker,
     infrastructure/state/cherrypicker/CherryPicker.SHIP.xml — see the
     comment there) and separately, `leutiankane.mines2patchouterrim`'s own
     Patch_Mines2.0OuterRim.xml adds a MinesAutomatedExtension.MineableSettings
     mod extension directly onto OuterRim_Tibanna (the ITEM def), making the
     raw item minable via the "Mines and Automated Mining" framework
     (researchPrerequisites OuterRim_HypertechFabrication, workOffset 200,
     mineableYield 10) — confirmed by reading that mod's patch file directly.

     This second route is NOT a standalone def — it is one <li> appended to
     an ALREADY-EXISTING <modExtensions> list on OuterRim_Tibanna's own base
     def (which also carries a VEF.Things.ThingDefExtension for deepColor,
     unrelated and left alone). Cherry Picker cuts whole (DefType, defName)
     pairs and cannot reach a single list entry inside a def the ruling says
     must STAY (the item itself is the one thing this spec keeps) — so this
     route is removed the same way WreckVerminNest_ShipChunk.xml fixes a
     defect inside a kept def: a scoped ordinary patch, not a Cherry Picker
     entry.

     Gate: OUTER MayRequire tests both ingredients — Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey
     is NOT required here (OuterRim_Tibanna is neronix17.outerrim.core's own
     item, not Odyssey's) — the real gate is that BOTH
     neronix17.outerrim.core (owns OuterRim_Tibanna) and
     leutiankane.mines2patchouterrim (the mod that actually adds the
     offending extension) are active; if either is absent this Operation is
     dropped at load and nothing dangles. INNER PatchOperationConditional
     confirms the specific <li> is still there before removing it — same
     discipline as every other patch in this folder, and load-bearing here
     because the owner's own ruling explicitly warns "LK's patches can no-op
     silently": if `mines2patchouterrim`'s own AddModExtension already failed
     for any reason, this patch's inner Conditional reports nomatch rather
     than silently claiming a removal that never had anything to remove.

     Load order: mandrake.rut.patches loads LATE in the campaign's full mod
     list (after neronix17.outerrim.core, leutiankane.mineablesor and
     leutiankane.mines2patchouterrim, all of which sit in the OuterRim/LK
     block well before the mandrake.rut.* tail) — confirmed against the live
     ModsConfig.xml, 2026-09-12 — so LK's AddModExtension has already run by
     the time this patch's PatchOperationRemove executes. Verify LIVE after
     any mod-list reorder: a patch that runs BEFORE the one it undoes
     produces the same "ran, matched nothing, changed nothing" silence this
     comment is warning about in the first place.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional" MayRequire="neronix17.outerrim.core,leutiankane.mines2patchouterrim">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="OuterRim_Tibanna"]/modExtensions</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationConditional">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="OuterRim_Tibanna"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="MinesAutomatedExtension.MineableSettings"]</xpath>
      <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
        <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="OuterRim_Tibanna"]/modExtensions/li[@Class="MinesAutomatedExtension.MineableSettings"]</xpath>
      </match>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
